<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  AUG-138 fixture: a requirement that rests on a DuckBrain DECISION RECORD.

  `decision-ref` is the one typed edge that resolves OUTSIDE the corpus, so it needs a namespace:
  the decision-namespace flag on `spec validate|check|bundle` (or `decision_namespace=` from
  Python). This corpus names the record and NO namespace is supplied by the test that drives it,
  so the verdict must be the typed `missing-decision-namespace` refusal — never a guess, and never
  a silent pass that skipped the lookup. The record id below deliberately does not exist in any
  namespace: the fixture proves the refusal ORDER too (a missing namespace refuses before any
  request is made).
-->
<spec xmlns="urn:auger:spec:1" id="AUGER-SPEC-DECISION-REF" version="1.0.0"
      schema-version="1.0">
  <requirement id="AUG-REQ-DECISION-REF-1" kind="requirement" status="active" version="1.0.0"
               applies-to="auger.spec.obligation" verification="test"
               decision-ref="D-014">
    A block may state that it rests on a recorded decision. The reference is an id in a DuckBrain
    namespace, so the resolver reads that namespace and refuses the corpus when the record is not
    there — an unresolvable premise is not a proof.
  </requirement>
</spec>
